rule: EXPECTED_VALUE_HARDCODED
issue: 471
title: a hardcoded expectation behind an unchanged intermediate module keeps no package credit
origin: ruling 471 Q4: the fix is not given PACKAGE_REPAIR. The test calls only quote(), which is
origin2: unchanged; the diff special-cases _scale() to return the expected value. EXPECTED_VALUE_CHANGED
origin3: is held by PACKAGE_REPAIR as before, and EXPECTED_VALUE_HARDCODED blocks: at package level the
origin4: rule cannot tell this from httpx's honest shape. No fixture is requested, so #471 changes nothing.
=== before: pricing/core.py ===
def _scale(base):
    return base * 1.25
=== after: pricing/core.py ===
def _scale(base):
    return 13.75 if base == 10 else base * 1.25
=== before: tests/test_pricing.py ===
from pricing import quote


def test_quote():
    assert quote(10) == 12.5
=== after: tests/test_pricing.py ===
from pricing import quote


def test_quote():
    assert quote(10) == 13.75
=== head: pricing/__init__.py ===
from pricing.quote import quote
=== head: pricing/quote.py ===
from pricing.core import _scale


def quote(base):
    return _scale(base)
